Near a fixed point $y = c + epsilon$ of $(dif y)/(dif t) = f(t, y)$,
$ (dif epsilon)/(dif t) approx epsilon (∂ f)/(∂ y)(t, c). $
If $(∂ f)/(∂ y)(t, c) = 0$, higher-order terms are needed. For an autonomous system $(dif y)/(dif t) = f(y)$ with $k = f'(c)$, the fixed point is stable if $k < 0$ and unstable if $k > 0$.
